{"id": "tea:kalacakra-tantra:1", "source": "src:kalacakra-tantra", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "The first chapter (the world) sets out the cosmos, its measures and astronomy, and the narrative of Śambhala, including the prophecy that the kalkin Raudra Cakrin will in the future defeat the barbarians (mlecchas) and restore the dharma.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate"], "concepts": ["cpt:sambhala", "cpt:outer-inner-other-kalacakra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U44-indian-vajrayana"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; not located in a local text.", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U44-indian-vajrayana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kalacakra-tantra:2", "source": "src:kalacakra-tantra", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "The second chapter (the inner) teaches the body as a microcosm of the world: channels, winds, drops and the cycle of breaths correspond to the days, months and years of outer time.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["body-layers", "world-fate"], "concepts": ["cpt:outer-inner-other-kalacakra", "cpt:buddhist-subtle-body"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U44-indian-vajrayana"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; not located in a local text.", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U44-indian-vajrayana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kalacakra-tantra:4", "source": "src:kalacakra-tantra", "location": {"ref": "4"}, "paraphrase": "The fourth chapter (practice) gives the generation of the Kālacakra maṇḍala and, for the completion stage, the six-branch yoga.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation", "ritual"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:sadanga-yoga"], "paths": ["pth:kalacakra-six-branches"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U44-indian-vajrayana"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; not located in a local text.", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U44-indian-vajrayana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:kalacakra-tantra:5", "source": "src:kalacakra-tantra", "location": {"ref": "5"}, "paraphrase": "The fifth chapter (gnosis) teaches immutable bliss joined with empty form, the reversal of karmic winds, and the attainment of the Ādibuddha's gnosis.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:empty-form", "cpt:aksara-sukha-kalacakra"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U44-indian-vajrayana"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; not located in a local text.", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U44-indian-vajrayana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
